# Security Rules

## Secrets

- Never commit `.env`, tokens, PATs, connection strings, or MCP auth headers.
- Never print secret values in chat responses.
- Use `.env.example` with placeholders only.

## Auth and data

- Preserve legacy authz: roles + `permissions_json` + business scoping from `source-app/`.
- Do not weaken password, JWT, OAuth, or permission checks.
- Parameterize all SQL; no string-concatenated queries.
- Do not log PII or tokens.

## Source tree

- Treat `source-app/` as read-only.
- Treat `source-app/backend/.env` and any MCP tokens as compromised if ever committed — rotate immediately.
